message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on the "SWASH" car-cleaning kit. I recall it being classified as a set under GRI 3(b), with the essential character given by the squeegee/sponge with handle. The likely heading is 9603 (brooms, brushes, hand-operated mechanical floor sweepers, mops, and squeegees). Subheading 9603.90 covers other items, with 9603.90.80 or 9603.90.50 as the statistical lines. A rubber squeegee falls under 9603.90.8050 or similar, but the sponge-and-handle combination suggests a different line.

Subheading 9603.40 covers paint, distemper, varnish or similar brushes, and paint pads and rollers. Squeegees (other than roller squeegees) fall under 9603.90, so the code is 9603.90.8050 or 9603.90.8010 if the bucket and squeegee are classed together. Since the tariff line "Other: Other" is 9603.90.8050 ("Other"), I'll use that.

